VBUS20 AT U3'S INPUT, UNDER LOAD AND TEMPERATURE, FROM THE DESIGN AS GENERATED (vbus20_range.py, stream l3plane,
MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: desk arithmetic, nothing built, powered or measured. Basis per figure: MAKER (document,
page, read from its text layer here), NETLIST, or INFERRED (reason given).

1. THE CIRCUIT (NETLIST v2/ecad/pcb-a-power-a23/out/pcb-a-power.net, sha256/16 6c40250c47195ebb)
   PASS the FB divider                     R6 240k 1% on ['FE_FB', 'VBUS20'], R7 10k 1% on ['FE_FB', 'GND'], U2 (LM5176PWPR) pin 11 on FE_FB
   PASS R11, the front end's ISNS shunt    10mOhm 1% 2512 (ISNS), pin 1 FE_OUT, pin 2 VBUS20: the divider's R6 is on VBUS20, the shunt's far side
   PASS U3's input                         R16 10mOhm 1% 2512 (RAC, input current sense) from VBUS20 to CH_ACN; U3 (BQ25731RSNR) pin 1 VBUS on VBUS20
   PASS no purchase code in the netlist    R6 None, R7 None
   So U2 regulates VBUS20 itself (R6's pin on VBUS20): R11's drop (FE_OUT to VBUS20) is INSIDE the loop and does not
   lower VBUS20. U3's VBUS pin and R16 sit on the same net; the copper between R6's tap and R16's pin carries U3's input
   current, and its resistance is a layout quantity.

2. R6 AND R7, THE PARTS
   the netlist carries no purchase code for either (fact 4); lcsc_fill.py's MAP (applied as that script applies it) gives
   R6 '240k 1%' 0603 -> C137765 and R7 '10k 1%' 0603 -> C25804; the released A24 BOM rows read R6 ('240k 1%', 'C137765') and R7 ('10k 1%', 'C25804') (agree)
